      "id": "GENUS_GERONTICUS",
      "name": "Geronticus",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Two species of bald ibis with completely bare, featherless heads — in contrast to other ibises which have featherless areas only on the face. They nest on cliff ledges rather than in trees. The Northern Bald Ibis was once widespread across Europe, the Middle East, and North Africa; its disappearance from Europe is one of the best-documented avian extinctions on the continent.",
